                          |CKBChapter 1 - How do I MUD?
                      |BKB-----------------------------------

|YKOA MUD is a shared text world. Player characters explore it alongside
non-player characters, creatures, objects, and other players.

The place around you is called a room. Start with |YKBlook|YKO, then examine
interesting details with |YKBlook <thing>|YKO. The room lists its available
exits; move by typing the exit name or a standard direction such as north,
south, east, west, up, or down. Common abbreviations such as |YKBl|YKO,
|YKBn|YKO, and |YKBe|YKO work too.

Useful first commands:

  |YKBinventory|YKO             Show what you carry
  |YKBscore|YKO                 Show your character and resources
  |YKBwho|YKO                   Show connected players
  |YKBfinger <player>|YKO       Read public character information
  |YKBcommands|YKO              List commands available to you

Speak in the room with |YKBsay <message>|YKO, speak privately with
|YKBtell <player> <message>|YKO, and ask the whole community with
|YKBnewbie <message>|YKO. If language causes confusion, use
|YKBset language common|YKO.

The help system accepts |YKBhelp <topic>|YKO. Use |YKBhelp list|YKO for its
sections, |YKBhelp list <section>|YKO for every topic in one section, and
|YKBhelp guide|YKO for a stage-by-stage path through the game.

Before traveling, review |YKBset list|YKO. Helpful options include
|YKBset autoexits on|YKO, |YKBset npcdetail on|YKO, and
|YKBset itemdetail on|YKO. Use |YKBmonitor bar|YKO for live health and
spell points. Screenreader users should run
|YKBset screenreader on|YKO.|000

